   "design": "Digital well logs carry well name, location and depth range in their file header, so the catalogue entry is filled from the header instead of typed. A reader proposes field values from contractor PDF reports with the page for each, and the technician checks every value. The catalogue can be searched by location, well and depth, so requests are found without browsing folders. Receiving files, scanning, shelving, error checks, sending, re-shelving, discussions and the lending book stay with the technician.",
   "approvals": [],
   "previous_blocker": "Headers and reports were retyped and files found by browsing.",
   "enabler_now": "Header import, PDF field extraction with page links and catalogue search.",
   "still_hard": "Old paper logs with handwritten headers.",
   "human_edge": "Knowing which old survey a geologist really means.",
   "ambition": {
    "kind": "none",
    "what": ""
   },
   "altitude": "Less retyping and browsing; the library stays.",
